    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0407" n="291" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg291"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1720.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Chargé Johnson.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-27T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1915—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Action reported in your July 22, 5 p.m., is commended. In view of the latest
                    evidence of this Government’s friendly interest the Department <pb facs="0408"
                        n="292" xml:id="pg292"/> confidently hopes for an early cessation of all
                    disorders and expects that diversion of funds will not be repeated. To this end
                    you should continue to impress upon the Government of President Jiménes the
                    necessity for a conservative and careful disbursement of revenues.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
